cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "voteworth: how many independent votes your LLM judge panel is actually worth"
message: "If you use this software, please cite the measurement note below."
type: software
authors:
  - given-names: Alexander
    family-names: Bering
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0009-0001-1793-012X"
license: Apache-2.0
repository-code: "https://github.com/zensation-ai/voteworth"
abstract: >
  Measures whether an LLM voter or judge panel can produce an independent majority, corrects
  the vote for correlated voters, and reports when it cannot. Voters drawn from the same model
  share their error modes, so a correlated bloc can win a plain majority while being wrong and
  have its agreement read as confidence. The package learns a per-voter independence weight
  from a vote history, or derives one from provenance labels when no history exists. It states
  its own boundary: on a panel that is one model throughout, the correction is provably inert.
keywords:
  - llm-as-judge
  - self-consistency
  - majority voting
  - ensemble
  - calibration
  - overconfidence
